- Story & Context: Under the relentless glare of the projector lamp in the silent Picture House, the veteran projectionist, Old Man Salazar, confessed his greatest sin to the flickering beam: he’d intentionally spliced abstract, disturbing footage of his own creation into the town’s wholesome newsreels, wanting to shake the complacent patrons awake, his calloused hands trembling slightly as he threaded the reel. "Did you ever truly see what was projected?"
